[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67479,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hamartoma of mature cardiac myocytes is a benign growth of differentiated mature striated cardiac myocytes.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67480,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67481,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67482,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> hamartoma of adult cardiac myocytes; cardiac hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67483,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67484,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Usually arising in the ventricles, hamartomas of mature cardiac myocytes have also been reported in the atria {18812338; 31374034}. They may be multiple or (more commonly) solitary lesions {18508110}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67485,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are asymptomatic and incidental at the time of autopsy or imaging (echocardiography, CT, MRI, and PET) {15746719; 31933959}. In symptomatic cases, the clinical features are often related to arrhythmia (palpitations, syncope, chest pain, and sudden death) {21354369}. Variable electrocardiographic abnormalities have been reported {18508110}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67486,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 50&nbsp;cases have been reported in the literature, with patient ages spanning 6&nbsp;months to 76&nbsp;years. Hamartoma of mature cardiac myocytes is most common in younger patients (median age: 24&nbsp;years), and two&nbsp;thirds arise in men {15067542; 18508110}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67487,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67488,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67489,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Grossly, lesions consist of firm, poorly defined areas of pale-grey tissue that look somewhat fibrotic. The lesions are usually &lt;&nbsp;50 mm, although a 90 mm tumour has been reported {18508110}. Tissue interdigitation makes complete surgical excision difficult {23041004}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T09:32:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67490,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are composed of enlarged, disorganized, striated cardiac myocytes with sarcoplasmic vacuolization and bizarre nuclei. They are associated with interstitial fibrosis and may be arranged in disorganized whorls or a herringbone pattern {9744305}. Fat and nerves may be intermixed. The tumours express muscle markers such as desmin, troponin, actin, and myosin. Ki-67 studies have shown the lesions to be non-proliferative {9744305}.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnoses include cardiac rhabdomyoma (but hamartoma of mature cardiac myocytes lacks spider cells) and cardiac fibroma (which lacks myocytes). The appearance actually closely resembles that of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, but hamartomas of mature cardiac myocytes are discrete and localized.</p>\r\n<p>The term &ldquo;mesenchymal hamartoma&rdquo; is used to describe lesions composed of blood vessels, smooth muscle, fat, and nerves within myocardium {20850353}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67491,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not described</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67492,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67493,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Discrete, nodular collections of enlarged, disorganized cardiac myocytes forming a myocardial mass</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Admixed adipose tissue and nerves</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67494,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67495,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 135,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although histopathologically benign, these tumours can cause death from intractable arrhythmias or sudden death {18508110}. Surgical excision (even when incomplete) has proved effective for tumours causing arrhythmia and/or obstruction {21354369; 23041004}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]